#: includes/classes/docs.php:324
#: includes/classes/docs.php:369
#: includes/classes/docs.php:374
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:998
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:1001
msgid "System Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:102
msgid "Check that the template for this event is switched on. A disabled template is silent by design and looks identical to a delivery failure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:107
msgid "Ask the recipient to look in spam, and check the sender domain matches this site. Mail sent as an address at a domain this server is not authorised to send for is usually silently discarded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:114
msgid "Replies sent by email are not appearing on tickets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:115
msgid "Customers reply to a notification and nothing shows up on the ticket, or new mail to the support address never becomes a ticket."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:118
msgid "Check that collection is scheduled and running. Mail is fetched on a schedule, so a stalled scheduler means a mailbox filling up quietly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:123
msgid "Check the mailbox credentials and that the host allows outbound IMAP or POP connections. A wrong password and a blocked port fail the same way from here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:128
msgid "Check the banned address list. A customer whose address was banned has their mail accepted and dropped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:130
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:578
#: modules/banemail/tpls/admin_addbanemail.php:20
#: modules/banemail/tpls/admin_banemails.php:18
msgid "Banned Emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:133
msgid "Read the collection log on Email Health. It records every run: which mailboxes were opened, how many messages were in them, and what each message became. A message that was read and deliberately dropped — a reply to a closed ticket, mail to a mailbox set to collect new tickets only — is named there, and looks like nothing at all everywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:144
#: includes/classes/docs.php:168
#: includes/classes/docs.php:306
#: includes/classes/docs.php:333
#: includes/classes/docs.php:362
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:145
msgid "Nothing is happening in the background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:146
msgid "Notifications are not going out, mail is not being collected, retention is not clearing anything, or an import or conversion has sat at the same number for a long time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:149
msgid "Open System Status and read the Scheduled work card. Anything marked Not scheduled or Overdue is the answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:154
msgid "If WP-Cron is switched off in wp-config.php, check that a real cron job calls wp-cron.php. That configuration looks perfectly healthy until somebody asks why nothing has been sent for a week."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:157
msgid "On a quiet site, WordPress only runs scheduled work when somebody visits. A site with no visitors has no scheduler — a real cron job is the fix."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:160
msgid "Check the queue for jobs that gave up. A job that failed three times is left with its reason on it rather than being retried forever."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:169
msgid "An attachment will not upload, or will not download"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:170
msgid "Attaching a file fails with no explanation, or a file that was attached cannot be opened again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:173
msgid "Check the folder permissions card. An upload that fails with no message is almost always a directory this site cannot write to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:178
msgid "Compare the file size against the upload limit the server allows. The environment card lists both limits, and the smaller one wins."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:183
msgid "Check the allowed file types. A rejected extension is a deliberate refusal, not a fault."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:185
#: includes/classes/docs.php:235
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:943
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:945
#: includes/jssupportticketadmin.php:199
#: includes/jssupportticketadmin.php:200
#: modules/aiagent/model.php:498
#: modules/configuration/tpls/admin_configurations.php:757
#: modules/jssupportticket/tpls/admin_help.php:54
msgid "Configurations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:188
msgid "Attachments are served through the plugin rather than by direct URL, so a link copied from the file system will not open. Use the link on the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:198
msgid "An agent cannot see or do something"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:199
msgid "An agent reports a missing menu, an empty ticket list, or a button that says they do not have permission."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:202
msgid "Open Agent Access and find them. It shows their WordPress role, their help desk role, the departments they cover and what that adds up to, in one place — which is usually enough on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:204
#: includes/classes/docs.php:209
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:393
#: modules/jssupportticket/tpls/admin_agentaccess.php:25
msgid "Agent Access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:207
msgid "An empty ticket list is nearly always department scope rather than permissions: an agent sees the departments they are assigned to and no others."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:212
msgid "Check the help desk role rather than the WordPress role. A WordPress administrator with no help desk role assigned still sees very little."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:217
msgid "If the menu itself is missing, the capability was never granted. Deactivating and reactivating the plugin reconciles roles and capabilities from a single definition and repairs it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:223
msgid "Customer portal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:224
msgid "Customers cannot reach the portal or their tickets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:225
msgid "The support page is blank, sends people to a login they cannot pass, or shows a customer none of the tickets they have raised."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:228
msgid "Check the page still contains the help desk shortcode. A theme change or a page rebuild is the usual way it goes missing, and the result is a blank page rather than an error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:230
msgid "Pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:233
msgid "Check whether guests are allowed to open tickets, or whether an account is required. Both are valid settings and they look very different to a customer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:238
msgid "A customer sees the tickets attached to their account. Tickets raised by email before they had an account, or under another address, belong to a different customer record."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:241
msgid "If the portal is styled wrongly rather than missing, the generated colour stylesheet may not be writable. The folder permissions card says so."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:252
#: includes/classes/docs.php:281
msgid "Migrations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:253
msgid "Importing from another help desk"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:254
msgid "Moving from SupportCandy, Fluent Support or Awesome Support, or an import that has stopped, duplicated something, or brought less across than expected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:257
msgid "Preview before importing. The preview counts every record in the source and, more importantly, names what will be dropped because the add-on that holds it is not active here — a decision to make before the old help desk is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:259
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:977
#: includes/jssupportticketadmin.php:237
#: includes/jssupportticketadmin.php:238
#: modules/thirdpartyimport/tpls/admin_importdata.php:12
#: modules/thirdpartyimport/tpls/admin_importdata.php:118
msgid "Import Data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:262
msgid "Take a database backup first. The import can be rolled back exactly, but a backup is what covers everything a rollback is not designed for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:265
msgid "An import that stopped part way has not lost anything. Every record it created is recorded, so it can be rolled back and run again — records already brought across are skipped rather than duplicated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:267
#: includes/classes/docs.php:272
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:989
#: modules/thirdpartyimport/tpls/admin_migrationresult.php:31
msgid "Import Report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:270
msgid "Read the checks that run afterwards. They compare what arrived against the source, and they are the reason to keep the old help desk a little longer or to retire it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:275
msgid "Do not delete the old help desk until those checks are clean. Once it is gone, anything missing cannot be fetched again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:282
msgid "A CSV file will not import"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:283
msgid "The importer refuses the file, or reports rows it cannot take."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:286
msgid "Download the template and compare the header row. Column order does not matter and extra columns are ignored, but subject, message and email must be present under those names."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:288
#: includes/classes/jsstadminsidemenu.php:201
#: modules/export/tpls/admin_csvimport.php:31
msgid "Import from CSV"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:291
msgid "A status, priority or department that is not one of yours is refused rather than swapped for a default. Check the spelling against your own lists — a whole file importing into the wrong department is worse than a file that stops."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:294
msgid "Dates must be YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS. A spreadsheet showing 14/03/2026 is usually holding something else underneath — format the column as text before saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:297
msgid "Save as CSV in UTF-8. A file saved in the spreadsheet's own format is not a CSV, whatever the extension says."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:300
msgid "Every row problem is listed with its line number. Fix those lines and import again, or import the good rows now and the rest afterwards — nothing is created twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:307
msgid "A table would not convert to InnoDB"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:308
msgid "The table storage card refuses a table, or a conversion run reports one it could not do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:311
msgid "Read the reason next to the table. It names the index and the width, and there are only two reasons a conversion is refused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:316
msgid "An index wider than the limit is a database that is old enough to cap index keys at 767 bytes. Upgrading the database raises the limit to 3072 and the table converts unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:319
msgid "A FULLTEXT index needs a database new enough to carry one on InnoDB. Upgrading the database, or dropping an index nothing searches on, both clear it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:322
msgid "Tables already converted are left alone and can be put back on the engine they came from. The data is identical either way — only the engine changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:334
msgid "The AI Copilot is not answering"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:335
msgid "A Copilot button reports a rejected key, an unreachable provider, or nothing at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:338
msgid "Press Test connection. It sends one short question and no ticket content, which separates a wrong key from everything else in one click."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:343
msgid "A rejected key is usually a key from a different provider, or one that has been revoked. Keys are never shown again after saving, so replace rather than inspect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:348
msgid "Could not reach the provider means outbound HTTPS from this server is blocked, which is common on shared hosting and has nothing to do with the key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:351
msgid "Every run, including the ones that failed, is listed with its reason on the Copilot screen. Start there rather than from the button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:363
msgid "Reporting a problem so it can be answered once"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:364
msgid "Something is wrong that none of these pages covers, and you want to report it without three rounds of questions first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:367
msgid "Download the debug file and attach it. It carries the versions, limits, scheduled work, queue state and recent errors — the questions that would otherwise be asked first. Passwords, API keys and licence keys are removed before it is written."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:372
msgid "Quote the short identifier shown at the top of the System Status page. Every log line from that page load carries it, which is how a report is matched to what the site was actually doing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/docs.php:377
msgid "Say what you did, what you expected, and what happened instead. An error message quoted exactly is worth more than a description of it."
msgstr ""

