#: includes/classes/workspace.php:838
msgid "One queue, scoped once"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:839
msgid "The list an agent sees and the ticket they may open are the same answer to the same question. Where the two are written separately, the gap between them is a ticket missing from the queue that still opens when its number is typed into the address bar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:851
msgid "The same tabs, meaning the same things"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:852
msgid "The front-end queue numbers its own tabs, and its tab 2 is Closed while every other part of the plugin reads 2 as Answered. A bookmark, a saved view or a support instruction therefore lands somewhere different depending on which desk it is opened in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:864
msgid "Assigned to me, unassigned, my team"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:865
msgid "An agent starting their day asks three questions in order: what is mine, what has nobody picked up, and what is my team carrying. A staff dropdown answers the first and can be made to answer the second by knowing which entry means nobody."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:874
msgid "One search across everything a ticket is made of"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:875
msgid "The backend has a single box that searches subject, message, replies, customer and reference. The front-end desk has a field-by-field search instead, so the same words find different tickets in the two workspaces."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:887
#: modules/jssupportticket/tpls/admin_developers.php:74
msgid "Filters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:888
msgid "Department, priority, status, product, help topic and date. Both desks have them; each builds its own field list, and they are not the same list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:898
msgid "A filter combination an agent uses every morning, kept by name. The views themselves are stored per person and are already shared between workspaces; only the backend offers any way to use them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:907
msgid "Bulk actions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:908
msgid "Close, reopen, reassign or transfer a selection. The backend has them and decides who may run them without asking the capability service; the front-end desk has none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:918
msgid "Columns each agent chooses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:919
msgid "Which columns a queue shows has been a site-wide setting an administrator makes once for everybody. A person working a billing queue and a person working a technical one want different columns, and neither of them is the administrator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:931
msgid "Raise a ticket for a customer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:932
msgid "An agent taking a request by telephone raises it as the customer, not as themselves. It is a permission of its own, and neither desk asks for it by name yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:941
msgid "Answer the customer, with attachments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:942
msgid "The verb the whole product exists for. Both desks have it and both post to the same task, which is why they behave alike today - and why moving one of them onto the service without the other would be the first real divergence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:951
msgid "Internal notes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:952
msgid "Written for colleagues and never sent. The permission is separate from replying, because an agent who may talk to the team is not necessarily one who may talk to the customer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:961
msgid "The timeline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:962
msgid "Replies, notes and everything that happened to the ticket, in one order. What an agent reads before answering, and the thing a reduced ticket page is usually reduced by."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1007
msgid "Close and reopen"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1008
msgid "Two verbs rather than one status change, because closing sends mail, stops timers and is what a customer is told happened."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1017
msgid "Merge duplicates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1030
msgid "Canned replies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1031
msgid "Both desks offer them. Neither asks the capability service whether this agent may use them, so the answer is whatever each template decided."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1040
msgid "Knowledge suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1041
msgid "Articles the ticket is probably about, offered beside the composer. Neither desk has this: the knowledge base is a place an agent goes rather than something the ticket brings to them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1054
msgid "One set of places to go"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1055
msgid "Home, queues, the ticket, customers, knowledge, reports and notifications. The backend desk has whatever is left of the administration menu after the refusals are removed; the portal has the control panel's grid of every layout in the plugin. Neither is a description of a working day, and they are not the same list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1067
msgid "A home to start the day on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1068
msgid "Personal workload, what has breached and what is about to, what nobody has picked up, where this agent was named, what they left half-written and what happened while they were away. Assembled today by opening the queue and sorting it four ways."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1077
msgid "Customers and companies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1078
msgid "Who has written in and what they asked before, scoped exactly as the queue is. The only customer list either desk had was the user report, which is a report - it answers how many, not who."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1087
msgid "A notification centre"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1088
msgid "Assignments, mentions, escalations, replies and approvals in one place, with preferences and quiet hours. Neither desk has one: there are three separate notification paths and none of them is a list an agent can read. Described here so the shape of the desk is complete; it is 4.5-UX-02's to build."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1100
msgid "Draft autosave"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1101
msgid "A long reply survives a refresh, an expired session and a closed laptop. The store is core and is already shared; only the backend composer uses it, so the same agent loses the same reply depending on which desk they wrote it in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1110
msgid "Keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/workspace.php:1111
msgid "Muscle memory does not know which workspace it is in. The backend binds keys; the front-end desk binds none."
